          "name": "Request an access token",
          "request": {
            "name": "Request an access token",
            "description": {
              "content": "This is the means by which clients obtain access tokens to use the service. You can see how to construct an Ably TokenRequest in the [Ably TokenRequest spec](https://www.ably.io/documentation/rest-api/token-request-spec) documentation, although we recommend you use an Ably SDK rather to create a TokenRequest, as the construction of a TokenRequest is complex. The resulting token response object contains the token properties as defined in Ably TokenRequest spec. Authentication is not required if using a Signed TokenRequest.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "keys",
                ":keyName",
                "requestToken"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
